<title>JAPAN: M'bishi 1996 domestic output down 9.6%.</title>
<headline>M'bishi 1996 domestic output down 9.6%.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mitsubishi Motors Corp (MMC) on Monday issued the following data for its domestic production, exports, domestic sales and overseas output in calendar 1996:</p>
<p>  Production	 1,200,007  down  9.6 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		 782,588  down 13.9 percent</p>
<p>  - Trucks &amp; buses   417,419  down  0.3 percent</p>
<p> Domestic sales	757,514  down  8.0 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		 363,242  down 20.5 percent</p>
<p>  - Trucks &amp; buses   394,272  up    7.6 percent</p>
<p> Exports		 455,498  down 10.0 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		 306,229  down 11.9 percent</p>
<p>  - Trucks &amp; buses   149,269  down  5.8 percent</p>
<p> Overseas output     721,854  up    5.6 percent</p>
<p>For the month of December, the figures were as follows:</p>
<p> Production	     99,799  up    3.4 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		  62,959  down  4.4 percent</p>
<p>  - Trucks &amp; buses    36,840  up   20.3 percent</p>
<p> Domestic sales	 60,983  down  3.7 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		  31,566  up    1.5 percent</p>
<p>  - Trucks &amp; buses    29,417  down  8.6 percent</p>
<p> Exports		  48,130  up    5.2 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		  35,211  up    9.1 percent</p>
<p>  - Trucks &amp; buses    12,919  down  4.2 percent</p>
<p> Overseas production  58,169  up   31.7 percent</p>
</text>
